[[File:Herblore.png|left]]
[[Herblore]] is arguably the hardest skill to train on an ironman since collecting the [[herbs]] and most of the secondary ingredients can be slow and time-consuming. Therefore, it is advised to put the rewards of every [[experience lamp]] and [[book of knowledge]] into Herblore if possible. By the time all hard [[Achievement diary|diaries]] are completed, if making all potions obtained along the way, the player should have around level 67–69 Herblore, just enough to start boosting to make ranging potions.

==Early training: Quests==
{{Main|Quest experience rewards#Herblore}}

[[Druidic Ritual]] is required for unlocking Herblore. Afterwards, some early levels can be skipped by completing quests that reward Herblore experience. Completing Druidic Ritual, [[Jungle Potion]], and [[Recruitment Drive]] rewards in total 2,025 Herblore experience, enough to get level 13. Questing alone will grant a total of 9,350 Herblore experience, elevating a level 1 Herblore to 26, granting the ability to make [[energy potion]]s without having made a single potion before.

* [[Druidic Ritual]] rewards 250 Herblore experience.
* [[Jungle Potion]] requires {{SCP|Herblore|3}}, and rewards 775 Herblore experience.
** For lower levels, infinite [[Volencia moss]] can be obtained from the rocks in this quest, and cleaned for roughly 1600 xp/hr, hopping worlds every 3 herbs. This might be of particular use to Ultimate ironmen.
* [[Recruitment Drive]] requires [[Black Knights' Fortress]], [[Druidic Ritual]], rewards 1,000.5 Herblore experience.
* [[Zogre Flesh Eaters]] requires [[Big Chompy Bird Hunting]], [[Jungle Potion]], {{SCP|Herblore|8}}, {{SCP|Smithing|4}}, {{SCP|Ranged|30}}, rewards 2,000 Herblore experience.
* [[The Dig Site]] requires {{SCP|Herblore|10}}, {{SCP|Agility|10}}, {{SCP|Thieving|25}}, rewards 2,000 Herblore experience.
* [[Shades of Mort'ton]] requires [[Priest in Peril]], {{SCP|Herblore|15}}, {{SCP|Crafting|20}}, {{SCP|Firemaking|5}}, rewards 2,000 Herblore experience, plus an additional 335 Herblore experience for giving the [[Diary (Shades of Mort'ton)|Diary of Herbi Flax]] to the [[Apothecary]] in [[Varrock]].
* [[Heroes' Quest]] requires {{SCP|Herblore|25}}, {{SCP|Quest|55}}, {{SCP|Cooking|53}}, {{SCP|Fishing|53}}, {{SCP|Mining|50}}, and many quests, rewards 1,325 Herblore experience.

==General information and tips==
Mid-level players may wish to kill [[Spitting Wyvern|spitting wyvern]]s for their high drop rate of 4-dose [[Prayer potion]]s. This method obtains [[ranarr seed]]s, [[ranarr weed]]s, and prayer potions at a fairly quick rate.

A long-term method of achieving [[stamina potion]]s for the [[player-owned house]] [[revitalisation pool]] is to always carry a clean [[torstol]] for the chance of a [[Jekyll and Hyde]] random event. Doing this significantly decreases the time required for higher tier [[Pool space|player-owned house pools]], but does reduce the number of inventory slots available. As such, it is best to do when doing activities that do not benefit from having a full inventory. As the torstol will need to '''cleaned''' before obtaining the stamina potion from the event, players will need to visit [[Zahur]] to have her clean the herbs for you.

==Level 3+: Cleaning herbs, making potions/tars==
It is advisable to work towards having access to [[Managing Miscellania]] as early as possible, since it is one of the best ways to get herbs passively over time. Training [[Ironman Guide/Thieving|Thieving]] to high levels is a quick way to get coins for funding the Kingdom; in addition to this, with high Thieving players are able to effectively pickpocket [[Master Farmer]]s for early herb seeds. When the kingdom is obtained, have 10 workers on herb farming at all times for the most effective yield.

After completing hard tasks of the [[Desert Diary]], [[Zahur]] in [[Nardah]] will make unfinished potions for 200 coins per potion (works with noted herbs and vials of water). [[Wesley]] will crush items that require the use of a [[pestle and mortar]] for 50 coins per item (also works with banknotes but does not require the diary completion).

